      <article class="doc">
        <h4>Payments</h4>
        <p>
          Every payment starts as a payment intent on the server, so the client never holds a secret
          key. <a>Checkout</a> confirms the intent; <a>Webhooks</a> record the result.
        </p>
        <h5>Payment methods</h5>
        <p class="doc__edit">
          <span data-k="old" data-gone>Checkout takes cards only. </span><span class="doc__gone" data-k="ghost" data-gone>Checkout takes cards only.</span><span class="doc__typed" data-k="ins-1">Checkout takes cards and Apple Pay.</span><span class="doc__typed" data-k="ins-2"> Totals follow <a>Rounding</a> <span class="peek__type">depends-on</span> so Apple Pay matches card totals,</span><span class="doc__typed" data-k="ins-3"> and calls <code>POST /payments/intents</code> for its intent.</span><span class="cursor" data-k="cursor" data-gone><span class="cursor__flag">claude-opus-5-5</span></span>
        </p>
        <h5>Testing</h5>
        <p>
          Use the test cards in staging. Apple Pay needs a real device with a card in Wallet, so
          <a>Testing</a> lists the shared phones.
        </p>
